  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/util.cc",
    "description": "`ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(const MonthDayNanoIntervalType&)` allocates the output using `buffers[1]->size()` but iterates using the untrusted logical `data_->length`. Unlike the other fixed-width endian-swapping paths, it does not bound the element count by the value buffer size. A malformed IPC array can therefore make `data_->length * sizeof(MonthDayNanos)` exceed the value buffer, causing out-of-bounds reads from `data[i]` (the reported crash at line 212 follows the unsafe load at line 210) and corresponding out-of-bounds writes to `new_data[i]`.",
    "conditions": "Provide an IPC stream with a non-native-endian schema so `context.swap_endian` is true, and a dictionary whose value type is `MonthDayNanoIntervalType`. Its dictionary record-batch field node must advertise a positive/oversized logical length while its values buffer is too short (in particular, a zero-sized buffer suffices). `ReadDictionary` loads this inconsistent `ArrayData` and calls `SwapEndianArrayData`; the specialized visitor then loops to the attacker-controlled logical length rather than at most `buffers[1]->size() / sizeof(MonthDayNanos)`, overflowing on the first element beyond the buffer."
  },
